<title>UK: UK's Whitecroft buys Siemens unit SLL.</title>
<headline>UK's Whitecroft buys Siemens unit SLL.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>British light fittings and building products supplier Whitecroft Plc said on Wednesday it had agreed in principle to buy Siemens Lighting Ltd, a British unit of German electronics and engineering group Siemens AG.</p>
<p>Whitecroft said it expected a final agreement to be signed after it had complied with a requirement to consult workers at SLL, a maker of road and commercial lighting fixtures.</p>
<p>In the year to September 30, 1996, SLL had sales of more than 17 million stg. Whitecroft did not specify the cost of the deal.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
